# ==============================================================================
# Mobile Application Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env and configure the values for your environment
#
# For development: Use your local machine's IP address
# For production: Use the live backend URL
# ==============================================================================

# Backend API Base URL
# ---------------------
# Development (Local Backend):
#   - For Android Emulator: http://10.0.2.2:8000
#   - For Physical Device: http://YOUR_LOCAL_IP:8000 (e.g., http://192.168.1.65:8000)
#   - For iOS Simulator: http://localhost:8000
#
# Production (Live Backend):
#   - Live Backend: https://ecochallenge-backend.onrender.com
#
# Note: Do NOT include /api in the base URL - it's added automatically by the app

API_BASE_URL=https://ecochallenge-backend.onrender.com

# ==============================================================================
# Network Configuration Guide
# ==============================================================================
#
# The mobile app needs to communicate with the backend API. The configuration
# depends on your environment:
#
# 1. ANDROID EMULATOR (Development)
#    - The emulator sees localhost as its own internal network
#    - Use the special IP: 10.0.2.2 to reach your host machine
#    - Example: API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000
#
# 2. PHYSICAL DEVICE (Development)
#    - Your device must be on the same WiFi network as your computer
#    - Find your computer's local IP address:
#      * Mac/Linux: ifconfig | grep "inet " | grep -v 127.0.0.1
#      * Windows: ipconfig (look for IPv4 Address)
#    - Example: API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.65:8000
#
# 3. IOS SIMULATOR (Development)
#    - Can use localhost directly
#    - Example: API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
#
# 4. PRODUCTION (Live Backend)
#    - Use the deployed backend URL with HTTPS
#    - Example: API_BASE_URL=https://ecochallenge-backend.onrender.com
#
# ==============================================================================
# Important Notes
# ==============================================================================
#
# - This file (.env.example) is for documentation only
# - The actual API_BASE_URL is configured in constants/api.ts
# - For Docker APK builds, use the BACKEND_URL build argument:
#   docker build --build-arg BACKEND_URL=https://ecochallenge-backend.onrender.com -t mobile-app-builder .
#
# ==============================================================================
